From 55d3ad2285c863b1de46966ef4891aae26168186 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: manishbazz <manishbazz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 22:37:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Particles bound to name text, Tekken-style punchy sounds,
 slow punch-in intro with sound
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- HomeParticles now accepts boundsRef and hugs that element's rect
  (inflated by a margin) instead of floating across the whole screen;
  particles drift upward and respawn at the bottom within that band
- Sounds redesigned with a percussive arcade-fighting-game feel:
  hover is a dry filtered-noise tick + short square blip, click is a
  bright noise snap layered with a descending sawtooth stab and a sub
  thump for weight
- Brought back the scale/blur punch-in reveal for the home intro, now
  ~2x slower (1.5s) with a gentler flash and a later underline sweep,
  paired with a slowed bass-swell + shimmer intro chime — this will
  actually be audible now since the entry gate unlocks audio first
---
